  "body": "Stacked on #1753 (merge #1753 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nAdd five original Haas machine definitions: VF-2, VF-2SS, Mini Mill, DT-1 and DM-1.\nRegister all five in the machine picker.\nState the requested travel, spindle, rates, changer pockets, holders, rigid tapping and flood M8.\nSet machine-coordinate Z retract to top home at 0.0.\nRecord public Haas sources and configuration choices in `docs/decisions/1976-haas-machines.md`.\n\nThe Mini Mill uses the requested 400 ipm feed and rapid cap from the redesigned EDU baseline.\nIt assumes the optional 10-pocket changer, flood coolant and rigid tapping are installed.\nThe current standard Mini Mill lists faster rates.\nLegacy Mini Mill and Super Mini Mill specifications do not define this entry.\nThe EDU page conflicts between its 8,000 rpm overview and older 6,000 rpm table rows.\nThis entry retains the 8,000 rpm requested by #1976.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe library had no definitions or registry entries for these five Haas configurations.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll three pins failed before the fix and pass after it:\n\n- `every_haas_machine_lists_validates_and_mounts`\n- `every_haas_machine_states_its_requested_configuration`\n- `haas_travel_feed_and_spindle_limits_are_inclusive_and_enforced`\n\nThe limit pin tests both travel endpoints on each axis and refuses travel, feed and RPM above their limits.\nRestoring the exact upstream `MACHINES` registry makes all three pins fail again.\nRestoring the fix makes all three pass again.\nA whole-module upstream replacement cannot compile on the older stacked base because it references the newer Waterjet kind.\nThe valid mutation restores only the registry constant.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed.\nAll 191 selected app binaries passed.\nThe UI library passed 816 tests, with six default ignored tests.\nThe selected UI integration tests passed all 25 tests.\nAll-targets clippy passed with `-D warnings` for `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui`.\nThe standalone Haas post processed the committed `full_circle.cnc` stream with each machine.\nAll five CLI checks reported zero warnings and zero swallowed blocks.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThese headless renders show the inherited Sinker EDM mode change from #1753.\nThe before view has five machine tabs. The after view adds the sixth tab, Sinker EDM.\nThese are the original parent renders, copied without changes to the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\nThey show the inherited UI change, not a new render of this review fix.\n\nBefore, 1280 px wide:\n\n![Sinker EDM mode before, 1280 px](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/742c9faaa14d94096fe0c45f6bbade9a0d8073aa/2123/before-1280.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter, 1280 px wide:\n\n![Sinker EDM mode after, 1280 px](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/742c9faaa14d94096fe0c45f6bbade9a0d8073aa/2123/after-1280.png?raw=true)\n\nBefore, 1920 px wide:\n\n![Sinker EDM mode before, 1920 px](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/742c9faaa14d94096fe0c45f6bbade9a0d8073aa/2123/before-1920.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter, 1920 px wide:\n\n![Sinker EDM mode after, 1920 px](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/742c9faaa14d94096fe0c45f6bbade9a0d8073aa/2123/after-1920.png?raw=true)\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical machine or controller acceptance run was performed.\nPixel snapshot lanes and release-only tests did not run.\nThe schema does not enforce the published 5,000 rpm tapping ceiling on DT-1 and DM-1.\nThese entries state rigid-tapping availability only.\nThe Mini Mill installed-option assumptions require a matching machine configuration.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#1753 changes `posting::MACHINES` and `every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration`.\nThis branch starts at its head, `c545e5fcd7dbc96f1a2dfaa6b535f96a3bf74ddd`.\nThe parent sinker template and UI changes remain inherited.\n#1681 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes `posting::op_streams`.\n\nChangelog: Add five validated Haas 3-axis machine configurations to the built-in machine library.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1976\n",
